wesh is a derivative work that condenses, merges and rewrites material from:

- caveman, Copyright 2026 Julius Brussee, Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/JuliusBrussee/caveman
  Used: caveman/ultracave voice rules, caveman-commit, caveman-review format,
  caveman-compress approach, caveman-explore/cavecrew-investigator (wesh-scout),
  native-core, lean-build, investigate-first, surgical-patch, safe-refactor,
  verify-and-stop, migration. All text was rewritten and shortened; no code copied.

- ponytail, Copyright 2026 Dietrich Gebert, MIT License
  https://github.com/dietrichgebert/ponytail
  Used: ponytail core rules, ponytail-review, ponytail-audit, ponytail-debt
  (shortcut: comment convention), benchmark figures cited in README.

- skills, Copyright 2026 Matt Pocock, MIT License
  https://github.com/mattpocock/skills
  Used: diagnosing-bugs, tdd (+ mocking), code-review (spec axis, smells),
  grilling, to-spec, handoff.

Optional integration (no code copied; wesh writes config pointing at the separately installed tool):

- codegraph, Copyright Colby McHenry, MIT License
  https://github.com/colbymchenry/codegraph
  Installed only with `--codegraph` (npm package @colbymchenry/codegraph@1.6.2) and used as an MCP server.

